
	Weatherfax module

The weatherfax plugin developed for SDRuno was rewritten for use with
sdrConnect.  The module is therefore a separate program, using websockets to communicate with sdrconenct. For Linux a so-called Appimage is available, for Windows an installer.

The module - when running - tries to synchronize with the start of a weatherfax transmission - using an improved synchronizer (a goertzel based implementation) to detect the start tone of the transmission. After detecting the start tone,
the data for the fax is read and converted to picture on a separate window.

The module is a separate program, using websockets to communicate with 
sdrConnect.  Important: The module assumes an input samplerate of 2 M.

For Linux a so-called Appimage is available, for Windows an installer and 
obviously, sources are also available.

Sources and a detailed description can be found at 

	https://github.com/JvanKatwijk/wfax-module

The AppImage and Windows installer can be downloaded from

	https://github.com/JvanKatwijk/wfax-module/releases/tag/wfax-0.6


